WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:08.720
I needed to do something in my community in order to complete the community service hours required to graduate from high school.
为了凑够高中毕业所需的社区服务时长，我得在社区里做点事。

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.090
Some of my friends had signed up to spend time at a soup kitchen, so I did, too.
我有几个朋友报名去施粥所帮忙，于是我也报了名。

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.540
It seemed like a good thing to do.
这似乎是件值得做的好事。

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:24.860
I thought that we would just be passing out dinners to those in need, but I found out we would be doing everything from preparing to serving the dinner.
我原以为我们只是给需要帮助的人分发晚餐，却发现从准备到端上晚餐，什么都得我们做。

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:30.800
We began preparing the food, from mixing salad dressing to separating frozen meat.
我们开始备餐，从调沙拉酱到把冻肉分开，样样都干。

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:38.070
Much still needed to be done before dinner was served, but already outside the building many homeless people were gathering.
开饭前还有很多活儿要干，可楼外已经聚集了许多无家可归的人。

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:43.890
It wasn’t until a couple of hours later that we opened the doors and began serving dinner.
直到几个小时后，我们才打开大门，开始供应晚餐。

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.970
As the line of people came toward me, I got a little scared.
排队的人朝我走来，我有点害怕了。

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.980
I’d come face to face with the homeless: How should I act?
我就这样和无家可归的人面对面了：我该怎么表现呢？

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.980
How would they treat me?
他们会怎样对待我？

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.860
Would they hate me for having more than they did?
他们会不会因为我比他们拥有的多而恨我？

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.630
While some of the people looked very friendly, some of them looked so dangerous.
有些人看上去很和善，有些人却显得十分凶险。

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.550
I didn’t have too much time to worry about it.
我没有太多时间为此担心。

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.490
I was assigned to serve the salad with the lady next to me.
我被分配和旁边那位女士一起盛沙拉。

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:14.770
She smiled at me and said if I needed help, she’d be right there, which I found quite comforting.
她冲我笑了笑，说我要是需要帮忙，她就在旁边，这让我觉得很安心。

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:18.140
I had never seen so many people wanting food.
我从没见过这么多需要食物的人。

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.110
They were of all ages and nationalities.
他们各个年龄段、各个民族的都有。

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:24.440
Most of them wore clothes that were torn and dirty.
他们大多数人穿着又破又脏的衣服。

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:32.420
Some looked like they had totally given up on life, while others seemed to be making the best of the situation, smiling and joking.
有些人看上去已经对生活彻底失去了希望，另一些人却似乎在尽力适应这种境况，说说笑笑。

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:38.110
Some were better off than others, but they all needed a good meal and a warm place to eat.
有些人比别人境况好一些，但他们都需要一顿像样的饭菜和一个温暖的吃饭地方。

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:46.010
It saddened me to think of how many people there were who didn’t have a place to call home and whose only food came from a soup kitchen.
一想到有那么多人没有一个可以称为家的地方，唯一的食物也来自施粥所，我就很难过。

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:50.700
As they came in my direction, I put on my brightest and happiest smile.
他们朝我走来时，我露出了最灿烂、最快乐的笑容。

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.790
I was so happy that I had earned my service hours in this way.
能以这种方式挣到服务时长，我真高兴。
